menu "WiFi Tool Configuration"

    config WIFI_TOOL_MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS
        int "Maximum WiFi connection retry attempts"
        default 3
        range 1 10
        help
            Number of connection attempts before falling back to AP mode.
            Lower values = faster fallback for testing and development.
            Higher values = more tolerance for temporary network issues.
            Default 3 attempts provides quick fallback for testing.

    config WIFI_TOOL_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "WiFi connection timeout per attempt (milliseconds)"
        default 10000
        range 3000 60000
        help
            Timeout per connection attempt before trying next network or retrying.
            Lower values = faster testing cycles and quicker AP mode fallback.
            Default 10s provides quick feedback during development.
            Production deployments may want 20-30s for slow networks.

    config WIFI_TOOL_RETRY_DELAY_MS
        int "Delay between retry attempts (milliseconds)"
        default 2000
        range 500 10000
        help
            Delay between connection attempts to avoid overwhelming the network.
            Lower values = faster testing cycles.
            Default 2s provides reasonable rate limiting.

endmenu